  "fibres": [],
  "measures": [],
  "notes": "Light reflected straight back into a laser destabilises it. Here a mirror sends the beam back the way it came; a 50:50 cube on the way picks off whatever returns onto the Back-reflection screen. The isolator (a polariser, a 45° Faraday rotator and a second polariser) passes the outgoing light and stops the returning light to its 40 dB extinction. Drag the isolator out of the beam, or turn it round, to see the back-reflection come back."
